From: Llaminar HIP graph kernel-argument ownership repair
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve final node-device argument geometry before graph pool sizing

Original construction and cloning copy kernel parameters before parent binding,
leaving the cached argument width at its default256. Packet capture consumes the
actual postLoad compiler/runtime width and alignment, so the underestimated pool
rolls over into additional allocations. Resolve each original kernel/device at
setup before recursive sizing, preserve its device across cloning, and propagate
metadata/overflow errors. Keep graph reserves, execution and public ABI unchanged.

Apply after the existing ordered HIP runtime patches at projects/clr.
Pinned upstream: ROCm/rocm-systems 6b0e43f341195e203754e08f850e437ff2fc09f9.
Exact development baseline: selected hip-event-lease-source; see package manifest.

